{"id":"torrey:olive-tree-the","source":"torrey","name":"Olive Tree, The","slug":"olive-tree-the","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Often grew wild — Ro 11:17.","refs":[["Rom",11,17,11,17]]},{"text":"In olive yards. — 1Sa 8:14; Ne 5:11.","refs":[["1Sam",8,14,8,14],["Neh",5,11,5,11]]},{"text":"Among rocks. — De 32:13.","refs":[["Deut",32,13,32,13]]},{"text":"On the sides of mountains. — Mt 21:1.","refs":[["Matt",21,1,21,1]]},{"text":"Canaan abounded in — De 6:11; 8:8.","refs":[["Deut",6,11,6,11],["Deut",8,8,8,8]]},{"text":"Assyria abounded in — 2Ki 18:32.","refs":[["2Kgs",18,32,18,32]]},{"text":"Kings of Israel largely cultivated — 1Ch 27:28.","refs":[["1Chr",27,28,27,28]]},{"text":"Green. — Jer 11:16.","refs":[["Jer",11,16,11,16]]},{"text":"Fair and beautiful. — Jer 11:16; Ho 14:6.","refs":[["Jer",11,16,11,16],["Hos",14,6,14,6]]},{"text":"Fat and unctuous. — Jdj 9:9; Ro 11:17.","refs":[["Judg",9,9,9,9],["Rom",11,17,11,17]]},{"text":"Bearing goodly fruit. — Jer 11:16; Jas 3:12.","refs":[["Jer",11,16,11,16],["Jas",3,12,3,12]]},{"text":"Grafting of, alluded to — Ro 11:24.","refs":[["Rom",11,24,11,24]]},{"text":"Pruning of, alluded to — Ro 11:18,19.","refs":[["Rom",11,18,11,18],["Rom",11,19,11,19]]},{"text":"Often cast its flowers — Job 15:33.","refs":[["Job",15,33,15,33]]},{"text":"Often cast its fruit — De 28:40.","refs":[["Deut",28,40,28,40]]},{"text":"Often suffered from caterpillars — Am 4:9.","refs":[["Amos",4,9,4,9]]},{"text":"Good for the service of God and man — Jdj 9:9.","refs":[["Judg",9,9,9,9]]},{"text":"Oil procured from — Ex 27:20; De 8:8.","refs":[["Exod",27,20,27,20],["Deut",8,8,8,8]]},{"text":"The cherubim in the temple. — 1Ki 6:23.","refs":[["1Kgs",6,23,6,23]]},{"text":"The doors and posts of the temple. — 1Ki 6:31-33.","refs":[["1Kgs",6,31,6,33]]},{"text":"Booths at feast of tabernacles. — Ne 8:15.","refs":[["Neh",8,15,8,15]]},{"text":"Beaten to remove the fruit — De 24:20.","refs":[["Deut",24,20,24,20]]},{"text":"Shaken when fully ripe — Isa 17:6.","refs":[["Isa",17,6,17,6]]},{"text":"Gleaning of, left for the poor — De 24:20.","refs":[["Deut",24,20,24,20]]},{"text":"Fruit of, during sabbatical year left for the poor, &c — Ex 23:11.","refs":[["Exod",23,11,23,11]]},{"text":"The fruit of, trodden in presses to extract the oil — Mic 6:15; Hag 2:16.","refs":[["Mic",6,15,6,15],["Hag",2,16,2,16]]},{"text":"Failure of, a great calamity — Hab 3:17,18.","refs":[["Hab",3,17,3,17],["Hab",3,18,3,18]]},{"text":"Of Christ. — Ro 11:17,24; Zec 4:3,12.","refs":[["Rom",11,17,11,17],["Rom",11,24,11,24],["Zech",4,3,4,3],["Zech",4,12,4,12]]},{"text":"Of the Jewish church. — Jer 11:16.","refs":[["Jer",11,16,11,16]]},{"text":"Of the righteous. — Ps 52:8; Ho 14:6.","refs":[["Ps",52,8,52,8],["Hos",14,6,14,6]]},{"text":"Of children of pious parents. — Ps 128:3.","refs":[["Ps",128,3,128,3]]},{"text":"Of the two witnesses. — Re 11:3,4.","refs":[["Rev",11,3,11,3],["Rev",11,4,11,4]]},{"text":"(When wild,) of the Gentiles. — Ro 11:17,24.","refs":[["Rom",11,17,11,17],["Rom",11,24,11,24]]},{"text":"(Gleaning of,) of the remnant of grace. — Isa 17:6; 24:13.","refs":[["Isa",17,6,17,6],["Isa",24,13,24,13]]},{"text":"Probably origin of its being the emblem of peace. — Ge 8:11.","refs":[["Gen",8,11,8,11]]}],"refCount":51}
